Root cause: two legacy postcore runtimes still treated News as their own section. remaining-sections-functional-preserve-v3 could rewrap the canonical News host together with legacy content, while remaining-sections could gate/hide the canonical host on navigation.

Fix:
- removes News from the legacy functional-preserve behavior; Access preservation remains unchanged;
- makes the canonical News runtime reclaim the direct page host and force-hide legacy sibling roots/loading/preserve wrappers;
- adds a narrow navigation reassertion guard for the News page only;
- preserves the #208 date filter, larger typography/contrast, 1360px layout, source links and active RONA_MARKET_NEWS authority model.

No backend/publication/IAM/Claims/Analytics business logic changes.

